        "date": "2026-11-24T05:25:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(bore): enter a Bore by plunge, ramp or helix, capped by the approach angles\n\nThe Bore op gets an `entry` field (plunge, ramp, helix). Plunge stays the\ndefault and is not written to the project file, so earlier files are\nunchanged. The links' approach `ramp_angle` and `helix_angle` cap every\ndescent of the hole.\n\nA bore that chose ramp or helix may take up to 4096 out-and-back legs on\nits ring (the 64-leg cap stays for the plunge bore), so a hole barely wider\nthan its cutter (a 3.2 mm hole, a 3.175 mm tool, a ring of 0.0125 mm\nradius) ramps at 5 degrees instead of diving. The Bore pane gets the Entry\ngroup; arc is refused by name.\n\nFixes #3828\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
